<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Emote</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>emote &lt;what you do&gt;
, &lt;what you do&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>emote is very VERY happy!
, waves at everyone.
</pre>
<p>This is a very useful command for talking with other players. The social 
commands (see <a cmd='#'>Help Socials</a>) are good, but they don't cover ALL the things you 
wish to express. Emote shows everyone where you are your name, followed by your 
words. So if Asta types emote is very VERY happy!, the others see:
</p>
<pre>Asta is very VERY happy!
</pre>
<p>A , at the start of a line is short for emote.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Socials</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Say</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Communications</a>
</pre>




</div>